{"content":[{"c":["BILHAH (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Servant given by Laban to his daughter Rachel when she married Jacob (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.29.29","r":"Gen.29.29","rawR":"Gen.29.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.29.29","value":"Gen.29.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 29:29"},"). Realizing her own childlessness, Rachel gave Bilhah to her husband as a concubine and accepted their two sons as her own, naming them Dan and Naphtali (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.30.3-8","r":"Gen.30.3-8","rawR":"Gen.30.3-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.30.3-8","value":"Gen.30.3-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"30:3-8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.25","r":"Gen.35.25","rawR":"Gen.35.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.25","value":"Gen.35.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"35:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.25","r":"Gen.46.25","rawR":"Gen.46.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.25","value":"Gen.46.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"46:25"},"). Archaeological investigation has confirmed the custom of a barren wife’s providing a concubine to guarantee children to her husband. Such an arrangement is mentioned in marriage contract documents dug up at Nuzi and dated from about the same time as the ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.29.1-35","r":"Gen.29.1-35","rawR":"Gen.29.1-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.29.1-35","value":"Gen.29.1-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 29"}," events. Jacob’s son Reuben was later guilty of incest with Bilhah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.22","r":"Gen.35.22","rawR":"Gen.35.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.22","value":"Gen.35.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"35:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BilhahPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 29:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.29.29","rawQueryValue":"Gen.29.29","sourceRefExact":"Gen.29.29"},{"anchorText":"30:3-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.30.3-8","rawQueryValue":"Gen.30.3-8","sourceRefExact":"Gen.30.3-8"},{"anchorText":"35:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.25"},{"anchorText":"46:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.25"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.29.1-35","rawQueryValue":"Gen.29.1-35","sourceRefExact":"Gen.29.1-35"},{"anchorText":"35:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.22","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.22","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.22"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7ef9520da4b835bf9e685c4c90c8ad11bf7a49356af5bec885474c644de13139","sourceItemName":"BilhahPerson","sourceItemOrder":316,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BilhahPerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bilhah (Person)","title":"Bilhah (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}